{"id":"nursing-home-staffing","title":"Nurse hours per resident day, from the federal daily payroll file","question":"Which Bay Area nursing homes report the fewest nurse hours for each resident, the largest weekend drop, or days with no registered nurse on the payroll?","finding":"Over 2025Q3 to 2026Q2 the middle Bay Area home reported 4.19 nurse hours per resident day; the California middle is 4.25 and the national average in the federal chain file is 3.9. 51 of 188 Bay Area homes fall in the lowest quarter of California (below 4.01); the lowest is Inspire Behavioral Health, San Jose, at 2.49. 22 homes reported at least one day with residents and no registered-nurse hours; Bancroft Healthcare Center, San Leandro, reported 98 such days. The middle California home's weekend figure is 3.83 (3.4 nationally) and its registered-nurse figure 0.50 (0.7 nationally).","how":"Every California row of the federal Payroll-Based Journal daily file for the latest four quarters was added up by home: hours of registered nurses (including directors of nursing and administrative nurses), licensed practical or vocational nurses, and nurse aides (including aides in training and medication aides), divided by the daily resident census in the same file. Weekend figures use Saturdays and Sundays; the weekend drop compares them with weekdays. A no-registered-nurse day is a day with residents and zero registered-nurse hours of any kind. Listed: homes below the lowest California quarter, or with five or more such days, or with a weekend drop of 15% or more; homes with five or more no-nurse days come first, then the fewest hours. The federal chain file names some chains after a person. State nursing-hours penalties (the State file's \"3.2 Nursing-Hours-per-Patient-Day\" administrative penalty) and all State citations since 2019 sit beside each home.","limits":"Hours are what the home's payroll system reported; a missed upload shows as zero hours, so a string of no-nurse days can be a filing gap. Small homes swing more. Homes that care mainly for people with mental illness use other staff who are not counted here, which is the likely reason a behavioral-health home is lowest. Hospital-based units and continuing-care communities staff higher for reasons of case mix. The national figure is an average across homes from a different federal table and may be adjusted differently; only the California file is on disk, so no national middle figure could be computed. Nothing here measures whether a home met the State's nursing-hours standard; the State's own penalties for that are in the column beside, to June 2024 only.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"city","t":"City","type":"text"},{"k":"chain","t":"Chain (federal file)","type":"text"},{"k":"residents","t":"Average residents a day","type":"int"},{"k":"hours","t":"Nurse hours per resident day","type":"int"},{"k":"vsState","t":"Against the California middle","type":"pct"},{"k":"rnHours","t":"Registered-nurse hours","type":"int"},{"k":"weekendHours","t":"Weekend hours","type":"int"},{"k":"weekendGap","t":"Weekend drop","type":"pct"},{"k":"noRnDays","t":"Days with no registered-nurse hours","type":"int"},{"k":"contractShare","t":"Hours from agency staff","type":"pct"},{"k":"hoursPenalties","t":"State nursing-hours penalties since 2019","type":"int"},{"k":"citations","t":"All State citations and penalties since 2019","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"home":"Bancroft Healthcare Center","city":"San Leandro","county":"Alameda","chain":null,"residents":36,"hours":3.63,"vsState":-0.145,"rnHours":0.19,"weekendHours":3.61,"weekendGap":0.007,"noRnDays":98,"contractShare":null,"hoursPenalties":null,"citations":null},{"home":"Pittsburg Skilled Nursing Center","city":"Pittsburg","county":"Contra Costa","chain":null,"residents":39,"hours":3.99,"vsState":-0.06,"rnHours":0.37,"weekendHours":3.72,"weekendGap":0.093,"noRnDays":9,"contractShare":0.008,"hoursPenalties":1,"citations":1},{"home":"Re